[00:15.74]1. Who is your friend, O God?
[00:20.58]Who in your tent may dwell?
[00:24.78]Who gains your friendship? Who gains your trust?
[00:30.16]Who really knows you well?
[00:34.90]All who embrace your Word,
[00:39.52]All who have faith in you,
[00:43.90]All who are loyal, all who are just,
[00:49.48]Living the truth for you.
[01:09.46]2. Who is your friend, O God?
[01:14.34]Who may approach your throne?
[01:19.22]Who brings delight and makes you rejoice?
[01:24.16]Whose name to you is known?
[01:28.72]All who exalt your name,
[01:34.04]All who your Word obey,
[01:36.18]All who are faithful, honest in heart,
[01:43.18]Truthful in all they say.
[01:51.00]3. Throwing our cares on you,
[01:56.02]Baring our hearts in prayer,
[02:00.70]Drawing us closer, bonding in love,
[02:05.44]Feeling your daily care,
[02:09.92]We yearn to be your friend.
[02:15.24]Long may our friendship grow.
[02:20.32]No greater Friend could we ever gain,
[02:34.00]No greater Friend we’ll know.
